    <bpmn:process id="W_W4208" name="W4208. Health, Safety &amp; Incident Management at Events" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Event operations; incident occurrence
Frequency: Per event (preparedness + reactive)
Volume: Per-event HSE (crowd, demo, DG, electrical, manual handling)
Owner: Event Lead / HSE (VS-24)
Participants: HSE (VS-24), Booth staff, First-aid/medical, Venue security, LP (VS-23)
Source: workflow W4208 — Health, Safety &amp; Incident Management at Events</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4208_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4208_Lane1" name="Event Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4208_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4208_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4208_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4208_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4208_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4208_Start3" name="Event operations; incident occurrence">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4208_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4208_Task4" name="Event Lead/HSE assess event HSE risks (crowd, live demos, DG, electrical…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Event Lead/HSE assess event HSE risks (crowd, live demos, DG, electrical, manual handling/assembly), and prepare controls (first-aid, fire-extinguisher, PPE, emergency contacts — links to VS-24.1)
Responsible (R): Event Lead / HSE
Accountable (A): Event Lead
Duration: Pre-event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4208_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4208_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4208_Task5" name="Event Lead/Booth staff manage on-site safety (demo safety, crowd flow, DG…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Event Lead/Booth staff manage on-site safety (demo safety, crowd flow, DG handling VS-114), and respond to incidents (injury, illness, security) per procedure (VS-24.2)
Responsible (R): Event Lead / Booth Staff / HSE
Accountable (A): Event Lead
Duration: During event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4208_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4208_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4208_Task6" name="Event Lead/HSE log/report incidents (investigation, records VS-88, insurance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Event Lead/HSE log/report incidents (investigation, records VS-88, insurance VS-26.3 if applicable), and capture HSE lessons for future events
Responsible (R): Event Lead / HSE
Accountable (A): Event Marketing Mgr
Duration: Post-event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4208_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4208_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4208_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4208_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4208_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-648 (ensure controlled execution — Exhibition &amp; Trade-Show Operations (PA-139.2).) | - CTL-648: event HSE risk-assessed &amp; controlled (VS-24); incidents logged/reported (VS-88); insurance where applicable (VS-26.3)
Owner: Event Lead / HSE (VS-24)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
